zac:BO0624_51192_lot_140 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "140 - VERY BEAUTIFUL WOODEN STATUE OF St. JOHN. Picardy,second half of 15th.century.  The head, with a charming expression, is inclined slightly to the right, and the pose is free and gracious. A heavy drapery, with folds elaborately carved, passes over the left shoulder, and is caught up on the right under the Saint's girdle. The left hand holds a book.  The right forearm is missing; the statue is otherwise admirably preserved.  Traces of the old polychrome remain.  (Illustrated.)  Ht.,45 inches." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_140_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <http://137.204.64.39/image/iiif/3/BO0624_51192!BO0624_51192_000611-p.%20[88].jpg/full/max/0/default.jpg> ;
