zac:BO0624_51192_lot_142 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "142 - GERMAIN PILON. France:I6th.—I7th.century.  Life-size marble bust, presumed to be the portrait of Diane de Poitiers. A delicately modelled drapery (strongly reminiscent of that of the Three Graces, by the same master, in the Louvre) is supported low on the breast by a ribbon which passes over the right shoulder, suggesting a quiver slung at her back. The wavy hair is drawn up all round the head and bound with a plait. On a base of green marble.  Ht.,26 inches.  (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_142_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <http://137.204.64.39/image/iiif/3/BO0624_51192!BO0624_51192_000631-p.%20%5B92%5D.jpg/full/max/0/default.jpg> ;
