zac:BO0624_51192_lot_25_title rdfs:label "LIMESTONE RELIEF. XVIIIth, dynasty. The head of the God Min, (whose whip is visible.) He wears a false beard, and a pectoral. A vase is presented by the hand of another figure. Both head and hand are exquisitely modelled.  Ht.,7 1/2 inches,W.,18 1/2 inches.  (Illustrated.)" .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_26 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "26 - LIMESTONE RELIEF.  XVIIIth.dynasty.  A figure from a procession. The body is human, the head that of an antelope, adorned with a long wig. In the right hand is the khopeche, in the left a lance. The left hand of the adjoining figure is seen, bearing an ear of corn; whence it is supposed that the bas-relief represented a feast in the honour of Osiris.  Ht.,22 inches,W.,17inches" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_26_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <http://137.204.64.39/image/iiif/3/BO0624_51192!BO0624_51192_000192-p.%20%5B15%5D.jpg/full/max/0/default.jpg> ;
