zac:BO0624_51192_lot_343 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "343 - FRANCESCO DA SANT' AGATA. Padua:about 1500. Important bronze plaque, in high relief; representing the entombment of Christ.  On the left, four Holy Women. The body of Christ is supported above the tomb by Joseph of Arimathea. Three bearded male figures on the right. Background of hills, trees, and the Cross.  A work of remarkable force;extremely rare. Cire perdue.  Ht.,63/4inches.Width,51/2inches.  (Illustrated.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_343_title ;
