    rdfs:label "352 - UNKNOWN MASTER.  About 1400.  The Emperor Heraclius. (Emperor of Byzance, 61o-641.)" ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_352_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <nan> ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_352_id ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://w3id.org/zac/type/medaglie> ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_352_description .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_352_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """352 — UNKNOWN MASTER.\r
\r
About 1400.\r
\r
The Emperor Heraclius. (Emperor of Byzance, 61o-641.)\r
\r
HPAKAEIOE ENXQ TQ OQ TICTOC BACI KAI AVTO PO NIKHTHE KAI AOAOO ETHC AEI AYTYCTOC. —-Behind the head:ATOAINIC,—Before:ILLVMINA VVLTVVM DEVS.- On creseent below bust : SVPER\r
\r
TENEBRAS NOSTRAS MILITABO IN GENTIBVS.\r
\r
Bust of the Emperor, crowned, looking upwards towards rays of glory; both hands holding his long beard.\r
\r
Reverse:SVPER ASPIDEM ET BASILICVM AMBVLAVIT ET CONCILIAVIT LEONEM ET DRACONEM.\r
\r
(Psalms, 90,13.) ——In centre :\r
\r
CIAAPASTYAAC KAIHAEYOEPQ/CE X ATION BACI HPA/KAE.\r
\r
The Emperor Heraclius seated in a four-wheeled chariot, drawn by three horses, led by an attendant. The Emperor holds a cross. Suspended above, four lamps.\r
\r
See detailed publication of Julius von Schlosser,on this,one of the oldest known medals:Die altesten Medaillen und die Antike",inthe Jahrbuch der Kunsthistorischen Sammlungen des allerhochsten Kaiserhauses.Vol. XVIII,Vienna, 1897. Beautiful old gilding. A perfect specimen of this excessively rare medal.\r
\r
From the arthur Labbecke coll.,Braunschweig. (Sale in Munich,1go8,No.1.)\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
\r
Diameter,33/4inches.\r
## 3-""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

