    rdfs:label """IAO BASIAILLA.\r
\r
Bust of Dido, facing right ; the hair elaborately dressed and bound with laurels.\r
\r
Reverse:\r
\r
(2I) ON. (2)\r
\r
A walled city, filled with fine monuments; the sea at its (Sidon,part of the realms of the Phcenician Queen Dido, at this time belonged to the Venetian gates, with three galleys. empire.)\r
\r
Specimen believed to be unique.\r
\r
Diameter,2inches.\r
\r
From the Maurice Kann collection. (Sale in Paris, 191o.)\r
\r
