zac:BO0624_51192_lot_354_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """Isotta degli Atti da Rimini; mistress, and subsequently third wife, of Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta.\r
\r
D.ISOTTE ARIMINENSI.\r
\r
Portrait, facing right.\r
\r
Reverse : an elephant (" one of the Malatesta devices : as a symbol of superiority to small misfortunes s"—— see G.F.Hill " Medals of the Renaissance " (pp. 45, 46.) Dated (M.C) (CCC.X (LVI).\r
\r
Diameter,33/16inches.\r
\r
See Armand, I, p. 21, No: 19. —Tresor de Numismatique. —— Friedlander.—Mazzuchelli.—L.Forrer,u.IV.——Heiss, IV, p. 44, No. 17 ; etc.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
\r
## 353""" ;
