zac:BO0624_51192_lot_518_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """518 -FRONT OF A CHEST.\r
\r
Ht., 40 inches.\r
\r
French,r6th.century.\r
\r
Finely carved, in three architectural compartments, surmounted by heads of angels. In the centre, St. Hubert; on the right, St. Martin; and on the left, St. Michael.\r
\r
Ht.,21 inches.Width,5 ft.3 inches.\r
\r
(Illustrated.)\r
