    rdfs:label "65 - COLOSSAL HEAD IN WHITE MARBLE. IVth to IIIrd century B.C.  Head of Artemis. Part of the waving hair is coiled up high on the head, the rest carried away on either side of the brow, half-hiding the ears. The eyes, full of life and interest, seem fixed at a distance, the lips are slightly parted. The nose is damaged.  (Illustrated.)" ;
