zac:BO0624_51192_lot_65_title rdfs:label "COLOSSAL HEAD IN WHITE MARBLE. IVth to IIIrd century B.C.  Head of Artemis. Part of the waving hair is coiled up high on the head, the rest carried away on either side of the brow, half-hiding the ears. The eyes, full of life and interest, seem fixed at a distance, the lips are slightly parted. The nose is damaged.  (Illustrated.)" .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "66 - MARBLE STATUETTE. IIIrd.century B.C. Figure of Venus, nude. A drapery is passed over her head, and falls to the ground. The expression of the face is pleasing, and the torso and thighs are beautifully modelled. One of the arms, which are damaged, supports the drapery. Traces of the action of salt water.  Ht.,14 inches." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <nan> ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_id ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_description .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_description a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label """66—MARBLE STATUETTE.\r
\r
Ht.,16 inches. IIrd.century B.C.\r
\r
Figure of Venus, nude. A drapery is passed over her head, and falls to the ground. The expression of the face is pleasing, and the torso and thighs are beautifully modelled. One of the arms, which are damaged, supports the drapery. Traces of the action of salt water.\r
\r
Ht.,14 inches.""" ;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300435416 .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_id a crm:E42_Identifier ;
    rdfs:label "BO0624_51192-66" .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_66_title rdfs:label "MARBLE STATUETTE. IIIrd.century B.C. Figure of Venus, nude. A drapery is passed over her head, and falls to the ground. The expression of the face is pleasing, and the torso and thighs are beautifully modelled. One of the arms, which are damaged, supports the drapery. Traces of the action of salt water.  Ht.,14 inches." .

zac:BO0624_51192_lot_67 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "67 - WHITE MARBLE HEAD. IVth. to IIIrd century B.C. A very beautiful head of a woman. Part of the crown of the head is missing, but the face is intact. The hair is drawn back to a knot at the back; the head is turned slightly aside, and the eyes cast downward with a sweet and melancholy expression. The mouth and chin, particularly as seen in profile, are modelled with much delicacy. Evidently the work of a great artist.  Part of nose restored in plaster." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_67_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <nan> ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_67_id ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://w3id.org/zac/type/marmi> ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_67_description .

