zac:BO0624_51192_lot_87 a la:Set ;
    rdfs:label "87 - BRONZE STATUETTE. Greek, IIIrd. century B.C.  An old bearded man, readily to be identified as Diogenes. He is moving forward, with a staff in his right hand, and a bowl in the other. His face has great character and expression. His hair is abundant, falling in thick locks. He wears a mantle, caught at the shoudler by a fibula, leaving the right arm bare, and falling to the middle of the leg in harmonious and supple folds. On his feet are thick-soled boots. Bronze pedestal. Green patina." ;
    crm:P102_has_title zac:BO0624_51192_lot_87_title ;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <nan> ;
    crm:P1_is_identified_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_87_id ;
    crm:P2_has_type <http://w3id.org/zac/type/bronzi> ;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by zac:BO0624_51192_lot_87_description .

